GUIDES={
'plan_draft':'Choose the current objective range containing the requested prose-writing instruction, not copied document text, layout directions or completion/finish instructions. Copy source_hash and select source_range start/end IDs explicitly; the host chooses no source. This creates a pending draft reference for a separate drafting step, not a document or literal source reference. Each new planning call replaces the active generation; preserve an already suitable draft instead of replanning. Provenance is checked, not semantic correctness.',
'plan_requirements':'Plan selected creation-proposal checks from exact unique source_quote passages in the current objective; copy source_hash and choose targets/constraints explicitly. Include supported explicit requirements; do not invent numeric bounds for literal text. Literal fidelity is checked by the content plan. Apply all-body constraints to every intended body paragraph. Use an empty plan only when none apply, never to bypass a mismatch. Each call REPLACES the active selected plan (at most8 checks); retain every wanted check. requirements=[] clears selected checks and records unassessed coverage. paragraph_index is zero-based among proposal body paragraphs, excluding tables and standalone page-break blocks; indices do not automatically track structural changes. Page units: twip, in, cm or pt; font sizes are points. The host verifies provenance, not interpretation or complete intent coverage. Metadata only: no document change, automatic correction or certification of later edits.',
'select_source_quotes':'Select quoted objective literals by q01..q24 ID and model-chosen role using source_hash; exclude formatting instructions. These IDs work ONLY here; creation uses returned ct_ references. The host assigns no roles. Use only complete candidates (at most24); for unavailable/ambiguous/oversized candidates, unquoted text or other user messages, load plan_content. If none are wanted, load prepare_creation or create. Draft requested prose during creation. Selection creates no document and does not certify complete intent coverage.',
'repair_content_plan':'Repair by original index; retain unchanged selections. For requested drafting, use defer_as_draft: remove its source-quote requirement, not the requested content; generate that text during creation. Do not ask users to approve already-requested drafting or choose internal indices or reference IDs. Replace copied selections only with exact source text; preserve uncertain literals, never shorten drafting to a matching prefix. Occurrence is a zero-based source-match index, not a band ordinal. Repair revalidates sources and creates no document.',

'delete_paragraph':'Remove one ordinary body or table-cell paragraph using its current target and expected_hash. Whole-artifact scope and its own batch required because positional IDs change. Refresh IDs afterward. Refuses section breaks, fields, tracked changes, bookmarks/drawings, removal of the last required paragraph, and removal that would join adjacent tables. Use replace_text for changing words without removing the paragraph.',
'plan_content':'Plan COPIED passages ONLY: quote text already present in the task objective (default) or a user source_message from this task. Never put newly drafted content in selections. Requested drafting needs no source quote; generate it later as plain creation text. Select each supplied literal paragraph or label separately with role paragraph/header/footer/table_cell; never quote the whole instruction. Layout, font and dynamic field instructions are not document text; do not join words across them. Omit occurrence normally: identical text at up to 32 source locations binds to all matches. Supply a zero-based occurrence only for a particular source location. For bands with page fields, select the exact literal prefix including source spacing; create configures page_numbers and separator separately. Error prefix hints are lexical evidence, not intent: never shorten requested drafting into a matching source prefix. Correct copied quotations from the existing source without reconfirming supplied text; preserve uncertain requested literals. References are source-hashed; planning neither edits a document nor proves complete intent coverage. Do not paraphrase supplied literals.',
'inspect':'Inspect source or target DOCX files with word.list_objects, word.find_text and word.read_objects. Use a verified file revision and bounded reads. Inspection does not authorize mutations. Load create again when ready to create a new target.',
'create_character_style':'Use word.stage_batch with one create_character_style operation; there is no direct creation tool. Read a verified style ID/hash as target/expected_hash. Supply a new style_id, name and only requested typography properties. inherit_base=true (default) requires a character-style base and keeps live inheritance. For an independent style set inherit_base=false: any verified style is an anchor, its properties are not copied and no based-on link is created. This also works when the document has no character styles. Requires whole-artifact scope. Existing styles remain unchanged. Load set_character_style separately only if assigning the new style was requested.',
'set_character_style':'Apply an existing character style to a nonempty text span using a batch operation. Read kind=style and verify its character type. Find/read the target paragraph at the current revision; use its hash and Unicode start/end offsets. Supply style_id without the style: locator prefix. Only the selected run style reference changes. Direct run formatting is preserved and may override style appearance; do not erase it unless separately requested. Text, hyperlinks and unselected run properties remain unchanged. Fields/drawings/tracked changes in the paragraph are refused.',
'refresh_fields':'Emit exactly one JSON object with three keys, each once: {"tool":"word.refresh_fields","path":"report.docx","revision":"CURRENT_REVISION"}. Copy the actual path/revision from current evidence; no operations array. Refresh saved native TOC and PAGE/NUMPAGES caches with word.refresh_fields(path,revision), under whole-artifact scope. The host paginates a private copy and transfers only verified field results; surrounding text, formatting, field instructions and unrelated parts remain unchanged. An existing TOC must be one supported top-level container. Page fields may be simple or paragraph-contained complex fields in the body or referenced headers/footers. Section references identify stories, never filenames. Shared header/footer PAGE has one representative cached value and still evaluates separately on each rendered page; do not flatten it into text. Locked fields, changed source content, ambiguous shared contexts and unsupported field structures are refused. TOC expansion changes paragraph IDs: re-read locators and review the new preview before Apply/Save.',
'format_text':'For one span call word.format_text (alias format_text) directly with path, revision, target, expected_hash, start, end, properties. No operations array or op field is needed. For multiple targets the existing word.stage_batch contract remains available. Format only a nonempty text span within one paragraph. Find the quoted text with word.find_text first; use a verified matching paragraph ID/hash and returned start/end. Read more context only if needed to disambiguate. Supply start/end Unicode-code-point offsets and properties containing only requested font, size_points, color, bold or italic. The text is not rewritten; unselected characters and existing run properties stay unchanged. Plain runs, hyperlinks, tabs and line breaks are supported; fields, drawings and tracked changes in the target paragraph are rejected. Offsets address the full paragraph text, not just a read excerpt. Use format_paragraph for whole-paragraph layout.',
'rename_style':'Rename the display name of an existing paragraph, character, table or numbering style. Discover kind=style and read the exact style ID/hash. Supply only name; style ID, assignments, inheritance, links, aliases and formatting stay unchanged. Whole-artifact scope required. Duplicate primary names are rejected case-insensitively. This does not change the internal style ID.',
'create_paragraph_style':'Create a reusable paragraph style in its own batch, without changing existing text or styles. Discover kind=style and read the desired paragraph base style; use its style: ID/hash as target/expected_hash. Supply a NEW style_id (letters/digits/underscore/hyphen, starting with a letter), human-readable name, and optionally properties with only requested overrides. Omit properties to inherit unchanged from the base. Existing IDs or names cannot be overwritten. Whole-artifact scope required. Read the returned style ID at the candidate revision; load set_style separately to apply it to paragraphs. No scripts or style XML.',
'replace_image':'Import the replacement through assets.import_image (import_image guidance is loaded with this operation), then copy its complete asset_id. Discover kind=image and read the exact target ID/hash. Submit replace_image with asset_id in its own batch. This replaces only image content, preserving frame, crop, anchor, wrapping, alt text and caption. Different source proportions may stretch within the retained frame: review visually and change geometry/crop separately only when requested. Other pictures sharing the old media stay unchanged.',
'format_image':'Discover kind=image, then read the exact image ID/hash with include_format=true. Use sparse properties: width_inches,height_inches,crop_left_percent,crop_top_percent,crop_right_percent,crop_bottom_percent,alt_text. For a width-only request, send width_inches and OMIT height_inches: the worker computes proportional height. For height-only, omit width_inches. Never calculate or guess the missing dimension. Supply both only when the user explicitly requests both dimensions; this changes the frame aspect ratio. Crops are percentages of ORIGINAL source edges, not cumulative; 10 means ten percent. Omitted crop edges stay unchanged; opposing totals must remain below 100. Crop changes the visible source region inside the unchanged frame; inspect the result and resize explicitly if needed. Zero clears a selected crop edge. Image bytes, caption and anchor/wrapping stay unchanged. Omit unrequested fields. Review rendered fit/pagination.',
'set_image_layout':'Read the exact image ID/hash with include_format=true. Use sparse properties for existing floating pictures: mode, wrap (square/top_bottom/none), horizontal_origin (page/margin/column), vertical_origin (page/margin/paragraph), horizontal_offset_inches and vertical_offset_inches (-22..22). Inline-to-floating conversion requires all six properties explicitly. Floating-to-inline accepts only mode=inline and removes floating placement/wrapping. Omitted floating properties remain unchanged. Aligned/percentage positions, tight wrapping and relative sizing are unsupported and rejected without flattening. Image bytes, crop and dimensions stay unchanged. Review rendered wrapping and pagination; offsets are inches relative to the chosen origins.',
'insert_image':'Insert an imported image as a new inline figure paragraph before/after an exact paragraph anchor. If the source is not imported, call assets.import_image(path) using the automatically loaded import_image guidance. There is no word.import_image tool. Copy its complete asset_id (image: plus hash); a filename is not an asset handle. Use asset_id from that receipt, width_inches (worker preserves aspect ratio), alignment left/center/right, required alt_text and optional caption. expected_hash is the PARAGRAPH hash from word.read_objects, never the imported image hash. Read anchor ID/hash first. One operation per batch; requires whole-artifact scope. Image bytes never enter arguments. Review fit and pagination. Refresh object IDs after insertion. For floating placement, load set_image_layout after insertion and read the new image ID/hash. Load format_image for subsequent crop/resize or replace_image to swap an existing picture.',
'import_image':'assets.import_image accepts a project-relative PNG/JPEG path and optional expected_hash from verified IMAGE source evidence. If no image hash is known, omit expected_hash; never substitute a document revision or guidance fingerprint. Returns a reusable project asset ID, source hash, dimensions and orientation; no image bytes enter context. This only imports a source snapshot, it does not insert or change a document. Placement is a separate operation. Keep EXIF orientation when choosing displayed dimensions; never claim visual inspection from metadata.',
'replace_text':'Replace a literal span in one paragraph using start/end Unicode-code-point offsets and text. Read text/hash first. Empty text clears a span, not the paragraph; for paragraph removal load delete_paragraph. Simple PAGE/NUMPAGES fields permit edits only outside fields; cached characters count in offsets but cannot be edited. Never cross fields or insert at field boundaries. Preserve fields, cached results and unchanged spans. Other field structures are rejected. Use numbering/styles/layout tools instead of text simulation.',
'set_style':'Discover kind=style and read the selected definition with include_format=true. Use its native style_id, not the style: locator prefix. Set style_id to an existing paragraph style ID. Changes paragraph style membership only; it does not define or modify a style.',
'format_style_typography':'Change only typography of an existing paragraph or character style definition. Discover kind=style, then read the selected style with include_format=true. Target its style: ID and exact hash. Supply only explicitly changed properties: font,size_points,color (six hex digits),bold,italic. Preserving a property means OMITTING it, even when the request mentions preserving italic or font. Never fill a default font or copy inherited values. For a request to change bold, size and color while preserving inherited italic, properties contains exactly bold,size_points,color; no font or italic. Use size_points directly, e.g. 14 for 14 pt. All paragraph layout and spacing are preserved by this tool. Character-style assignments and inheritance are preserved; table/numbering styles are not supported by this typography operation. Requires whole-artifact scope; affects every use and inherited styles. Existing direct formatting can override the result. Review affected pages.',
'format_style':'Change an existing paragraph STYLE DEFINITION, affecting every use including inherited styles; whole-artifact scope required. Discover kind=style and read include_format=true. Target the style: locator and exact style hash, not a paragraph. Use properties with only requested fields: font,size_points (requested point size; worker converts),color (six hex digits),bold,italic,alignment (left/center/right/both),spacing_before_twips,spacing_after_twips,left_indent_twips,right_indent_twips,first_line_twips (negative hanging),keep_with_next,keep_lines,page_break_before. Omit every unrequested field; do not fill defaults or reset spacing. size_half_points is a legacy alternative; never send both size representations. Omitted properties, inheritance links and paragraph memberships stay unchanged. Direct formatting may override the style. Review all affected pages. This does not create or rename styles.',
'format_paragraph':'Use properties containing only requested changes: alignment left/center/right/both; spacing_before_twips,spacing_after_twips,left_indent_twips,right_indent_twips,first_line_twips (negative hanging); keep_with_next,keep_lines,page_break_before; font,size_points,color (six hex digits),bold,italic. Typography covers the whole paragraph, not a substring. Omitted properties stay unchanged. Inspect include_format=true when needed. Use size_points for requested point sizes; size_half_points is the legacy alternative, never send both.',
'insert_paragraphs':'Use position before/after and paragraphs=[{"text":"only new content","style":"existing style ID","page_break_before":false}]. Read the user-requested paragraph/table anchor first; do not infer it from an example. At most 24 paragraphs, one insertion operation per batch. Requires whole-artifact scope. Reuse styles and refresh positional IDs after insertion.',
'set_cell_text':'Target an exact cell ID, not its paragraph. Supply text with only the new entire cell value. Newlines separate paragraphs. Complex cells (fields, links, nested tables) are refused. Use paragraph span replacement when preserving mixed inline formatting. Refresh paragraph IDs if the paragraph count changes. A cell selection authorizes this exact cell only; a table selection does not authorize its cells. Mixed cell and paragraph annotations require a separate cell-scoped task or explicit whole-artifact scope before this operation.',
'insert_table':'Insert a new table before/after an exact body paragraph anchor. Copy target and expected_hash exactly from the anchor search/read result; never invent or shorten hashes. rows is an array of arrays of cell strings, for example [["Label","Value"],["Item","100"]], never pipe-separated row strings or objects. Use the user-requested cell text, not example values. Supply explicit column_widths_twips (1440 per inch), header_row and an existing paragraph style. Up to 20 rows and 12 columns within the batch budget. Whole-artifact scope and its own batch required. The worker adds a separator paragraph if necessary to keep adjacent tables distinct. Review widths and pagination; refresh IDs after insertion.',
'insert_rows':'Read an exact row anchor. Use position before/after, rows=[["new cell 1","new cell 2"]],header_row=false. One value per physical anchor cell; at most eight rows. Copies anchor row/cell layout. One operation per batch; whole-artifact scope required. Refresh positional IDs afterwards. Vertical-merge insertion is not yet supported.',
'set_section_layout':'Read kind=section with include_format=true. Use properties with requested width_twips,height_twips (supply both to resize),top_twips,bottom_twips,left_twips,right_twips,header_twips,footer_twips,gutter_twips. 1440 twips/inch; orientation follows dimensions. Missing geometry must be resolved explicitly. Whole-artifact scope and pagination review required.',
'unmerge_cells':'Restore separate grid cells in one merged region. Discover kind=cell and read include_format=true; target the merged top-left cell ID/hash, never a vertical continuation. Uses the existing table grid, up to 20 rows and 12 columns. Content remains in the physical cells currently holding it; newly created cells are empty. It cannot reconstruct original pre-merge cell values: use Undo for exact prior-state restoration. Native grid-span/vertical merges are supported; legacy merges, mismatched continuations and tracked cell properties are refused. Whole-artifact scope and a standalone word.stage_batch operation are required. Refresh locators and review the region.',
'merge_cells':'Merge an unmerged rectangular region inside one exact table. Read the table and discover its rows/cells before choosing coordinates. include_format=true reports table grid dimensions and row/cell zero-based row_index and column_start; use that evidence, not global locator numbers. Use zero-based row_start/column_start plus row_count/column_count, up to 20 by 12 cells. Target the table ID/hash, not a cell. Whole-artifact scope and a standalone batch are required. All selected paragraph content moves in row-major order to the top-left cell; the merged area uses top-left cell formatting. Unselected cells and table grid stay unchanged. Existing intersecting merges, wrapped content, tracked changes and complex fields are refused. Refresh IDs and review the full merged area afterwards.',
'format_row':'Discover kind=row (optionally parent=table ID), match previews and copy each row ID/hash. Read include_format=true for existing layout. Use only requested properties: height={"twips":480,"rule":"at_least"} (1440 twips/inch; exact may clip text), repeat_header=true/false, allow_split=true/false. Repeating headers must be a contiguous prefix: enable top-down and disable bottom-up. Batch independent rows with separate operation objects. Text, cells, widths, merges and other rows stay unchanged. Review pagination; very tall rows may still overflow a page.',
'format_cell':'Discover cells directly with {"tool":"word.list_objects","path":"active DOCX path","revision":"current revision","kind":"cell","limit":20}. Match cell previews to the requested text; paginate or use a table parent to disambiguate. Do not start with paragraph text search for a cell-format request. Copy each matched cell ID and its OWN hash exactly; never reuse another cell hash. Read with word.read_objects and include_format=true when current formatting is needed. Always use the word. prefix on discovery/read tools. Use properties with only requested changes: fill (six hex digits for solid shading, or auto for automatic background), vertical_alignment (top/center/bottom), padding_top_twips/padding_bottom_twips/padding_left_twips/padding_right_twips (1440 twips per inch). Setting fill explicitly replaces cell shading patterns/theme values; omitted shading remains untouched. No text, widths, borders or merges are changed. Batch distinct cells using their individual hashes. A selected cell authorizes only that cell, not neighbouring cells or the parent table. Merged cells are physical cells; discover their structure and review the complete merged area.',
'format_table':'Read an exact table with include_format=true. Complete call shape: {"tool":"word.stage_batch","path":"active DOCX path","revision":"document revision from read","operations":[{"id":"layout","op":"format_table","target":"table ID from read","expected_hash":"table hash from read","properties":{"alignment":"center","column_widths":{"unit":"in","values":[2.5,1.5]},"padding_top_twips":80,"padding_bottom_twips":80}}]}. Replace example values with the requested ones; properties is ONE object. Use only requested properties: alignment left/center/right; column_widths={"unit":"in","values":[2.5,1.5]} with USER values and unit in/cm/pt/twip (worker converts); padding_top_twips,padding_bottom_twips,padding_left_twips,padding_right_twips. No nested padding object. One width per existing grid column. Only if requested, borders={"style":"single","color":"17365D","size_eighth_points":8}; style single/double/dashed/dotted/nil. Omit borders when preserving them. Direct cell overrides stay unchanged; review rendered fit.',
'set_list':'NEVER type list numbers or bullets into paragraph text. Two DIFFERENT objects are required: first discover kind=numbering and read the chosen definition with include_format=true; then call word.list_objects with kind=paragraph, find the user-requested paragraph and read its ID. Use the paragraph ID/hash as the edit target, never the numbering ID/hash. Set number_id to the discovered native list ID and level to a defined index 0–8. These fields belong directly on the operation, not in properties. Reusing the ID continues numbering. Optional restart_at=1..32767 creates a fresh instance for this paragraph only; requires level=0 and a resolved single-level decimal list. Read the returned number_id, then explicitly assign it to subsequent requested paragraphs to continue. Original list definitions remain intact; multilevel/style-linked/tracked restarts are refused. Omit restart_at for continuation. number_id=0,level=0 removes markers including inherited numbering. Preserve all text. Complete call shape: {"tool":"word.stage_batch","path":"active DOCX path","revision":"document revision from read","operations":[{"id":"list","op":"set_list","target":"paragraph ID from read","expected_hash":"paragraph hash from read","number_id":2,"level":0}]}. Obtain real IDs/hashes through list/read before emitting this call; never invent them or emit a bare operation.',
'repair_creation':'Repair a retained rejected creation without resending it. Copy cr_ and declare exactly the missing style IDs using requested typography. Optional bindings is a list of {"slot":"footer.text","ref":"ct_..."} objects: existing text slots and current active same-role references, at most24 unique slots. Do not add text or redeclare existing styles. Bindings confirm identical text/ref or fill empty slots; they never replace competing content. Revise text explicitly first. Omit bindings to preserve text. Existing styles, unselected content, fields, separators and layout stay unchanged. Compare proposed literals with the active plan; previews are navigation, not replacement text. Full validation precedes staging; only the user Apply/Saves.',
'create':'word.create creates a new DOCX once; revision=null. Text/cells: source {"ref":"ct_..."} or requested drafting strings.\nDeclare top-level styles; blocks/bands use their IDs (Normal built in). Use size_points OR size_half_points. Lists: paragraph list_kind; tables: rectangular rows. Breaks: page_break_before on the next paragraph, or kind=page_break between blocks; never leading/trailing/consecutive.\nGeometry uses twips (1440/inch); A4 portrait=11906x16838. Page fields: text="Page ", page_numbers="current_total", separator=" of "; never fixed totals.\nTOC: kind=table_of_contents, max_level=3, with a style\'s heading_level in range; a heading name is insufficient. PDF evaluates fields; refresh_fields updates saved caches only when requested. Disclose explicitly deferred refresh.\n24 blocks/32 KiB maximum. Continue with insert_paragraphs/current locators; never recreate/shorten. Worker adds a pre-table layout anchor.\nheader/footer=default/odd. first_header/first_footer enable first-page bands; even_header/even_footer enable even-page bands. Either switch affects both bands; omitted counterpart stays blank, never copied. Section linking/editing is separate.'}

GUIDES['prepare_creation']=GUIDES['create'].replace('word.create creates a new DOCX once; revision=null.', 'word.prepare_creation retains a proposal, not a file; revision=null. Review returned facts before finalize_creation.')
GUIDES['finalize_creation']=GUIDES['repair_creation'].replace('Repair a retained rejected creation', 'Finalize a retained creation proposal')+' Supply styles=[] when no declarations are missing. For other content/design changes load revise_creation; prepare_creation replaces the whole proposal.'

GUIDES['revise_creation']='Edit a retained proposal before staging. Supply its current cr_ ref and 1–24 changes: op=set/remove/insert, dot path such as styles, styles.0.size_points or header.style, and value for set/insert. Indices are zero-based. insert at styles.N appends when N=explicit count; set styles replaces all declarations. Implicit Normal has no index. Only content/design roots (blocks, styles, page, bands, literal_refs) can change; target path/revision/tool cannot. Omitted content remains exact. Full proposal validation is atomic. Returns a new proposal handle; review then finalize_creation. Never resend unchanged blocks to change typography.'

GUIDES['edit_creation_blocks']='Edit the current retained proposal, not a document: 1–4 changes indexed against the original proposal ref, never shifted by removals. remove_block deletes the chosen zero-based block. set_paragraph changes only supplied text, style or page_break_before on an existing paragraph; omit unchanged properties. Do not remove and set the same block or repeat a property. No automatic pagination or correction. Review the new ref before finalizing. For any other content/design changes explicitly load revise_creation; prepare_creation replaces the whole proposal atomically.'

GUIDES['edit_creation_styles']='Edit named style declarations in the current retained proposal using its cr_ ref and 1–4 changes. Use op=declare for a new style with its exact id, font and size_points; implicit Normal may be explicitly declared. Use op=update only for an existing explicit style ID, supplying only changed font, size_points, bold, italic or color. Omitted properties stay unchanged. Declaration and update are distinct: no automatic creation on update, no replacement on declaration, and no automatic paragraph assignment. To assign a style, separately load edit_creation_blocks and set the requested paragraph style. Review the returned proposal ref before finalizing; no document is created by this operation.'

